{"name":"Cold Pressed","hex":"#665b42","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"cold-pressed","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Alternative form of coldpressed."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["simple past and past participle of cold-press"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/cold-pressed"}],"entries":[{"title":"Cold-pressed juice","blocks":[{"text":"Cold-pressed juice is juice that uses a hydraulic press to extract juice from fruit and vegetables, as opposed to other methods such as centrifugal or single auger."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/ba/BluePrint_Cold_Pressed_Juice.jpg/330px-BluePrint_Cold_Pressed_Juice.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cold-pressed_juice"},{"title":"Cold","blocks":[{"text":"Cold is the presence of low temperature, especially in the atmosphere. In common usage, cold is often a subjective perception. A lower bound to temperature is absolute zero, defined as 0.00 K on the Kelvin scale, an absolute thermodynamic temperature scale. This corresponds to −273.15 °C on the Celsius scale, −459.67 °F on the Fahrenheit scale, and 0.00 °R on the Rankine scale."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d5/Antarctic_iceberg%2C_2001_-2.jpg/330px-Antarctic_iceberg%2C_2001_-2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cold"},{"title":"Pressed","blocks":[{"text":"Pressed is a 2011 Canadian crime drama film directed by Justin Donnelly and starring Luke Goss, Tyler Johnston, Jeffrey Ballard, and Michael Eklund. It is the debut directing project for Justin Donnelly."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/7/7b/Pressed_--_movie_poster.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pressed"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9c/Diving_signal_cold.jpg/500px-Diving_signal_cold.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9c/Diving_signal_cold.jpg/500px-Diving_signal_cold.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Signal \"cold\" – unofficial (except recommended by CMAS), it is nonetheless used by many schools of diving and propagated through diving websites as one of the more useful additional signals[1]","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ADiving_signal_cold.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/23/Goose_bumps.jpg/500px-Goose_bumps.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/23/Goose_bumps.jpg/500px-Goose_bumps.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Goose bumps, a common physiological response to cold, aiming to reduce the loss of body heat in a cold environment","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AGoose_bumps.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/bd/AntarcticaDomeCSnow.jpg/500px-AntarcticaDomeCSnow.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/bd/AntarcticaDomeCSnow.jpg/500px-AntarcticaDomeCSnow.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A photograph of the snow surface at Dome C Station, Antarctica. A part of the notoriously cold Polar Plateau, it is representative of the majority of the continent's surface.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AAntarcticaDomeCSnow.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/29/L%C3%A9on_Perrault%2C_1890_-_Out_in_the_Cold.jpg/500px-L%C3%A9on_Perrault%2C_1890_-_Out_in_the_Cold.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&